    "millsfield:images_texts": [
      "Effective DECEMBER 1, 1940\nThe\nTWA\nTRANSCONTINENTAL\nAirline\nThe TRANSCONTINENTAL Airline-\nTo\nFly\nAIRLINES\nTICKET OFFICE\n1339 WALNUT STREET\nINFORMATION - TICKETS - ALL LINES\nNO CHARGE FOR DELIVERY\nCall *\u003e PENNYpacker 1877\n4• ENGINE\nStratoliners\nLARGEST... FASTEST... COAST-TO-COAST",
      "OVER THE NATION'S MOST SCENIC AIR ROUTE\nShortest, Fastest, Coast-to-Coast\nOnly TWA flies the nation's most\nscenic air route over sunny western wonder-\nlands. See the heart of the Indian\nCountry, the Painted Desert, Grand Canyon and Boulder\nDam from TWA's luxurious Skyclubs and Skysleepers.\nYou get there faster-see more on the way-when you fly the\nRoute of the Stratoliners. TWA's scenic coast-to-coast route\ntakes no extra time—and there is no extra fare for scenic \"extras.\"\nWICHITA\nKANSAS CITY\nGrand Canyon\nNew Mexico\nCalifornia\nHARRISBURG\nPITTSBURG WASHINGTON\nLOS ANGELES\nFRESNO KES\nBOULDER DAM\nGRAND CANYON\nWINSLOW\nPHILHI\nI TWA System\n- Connecting Lines\n=- Other Lines\nArizona"
